'Subject: re : meter 5848\r\nvance ,\r\nwhat is the price and volume that should be entered for october ? apparently ,\r\nengage changed their name to coastal was the reason the deal ticket was\r\ncreated that way .\r\nbob\r\nvance l taylor\r\n10 / 11 / 2000 02 : 47 pm\r\nto : robert cotten / hou / ect @ ect\r\ncc : pat clynes / corp / enron @ enron , daren j farmer / hou / ect @ ect , aimee\r\nlannou / hou / ect @ ect , melissa graves / hou / ect @ ect\r\nsubject : re : meter 5848\r\nbob ,\r\nyou are correct , i did request a ticket at meter 5848 as a spot purchase .\r\nhowever , i \' m not sure why the ticket was created in the name of coastal ; it\r\nshould have been in the name engage energy us , lp . as for october , hplc is\r\nbuying this package of gas on a \" spot \" basis and a ticket should be created\r\nand entered in to sitara .\r\nthanks ,\r\nvlt\r\nx 3 - 6353\r\nenron north america corp .\r\nfrom : robert cotten 10 / 11 / 2000 11 : 12 am\r\nto : vance l taylor / hou / ect @ ect\r\ncc : pat clynes / corp / enron @ enron , daren j farmer / hou / ect @ ect , aimee\r\nlannou / hou / ect @ ect\r\nsubject : meter 5848\r\nvance ,\r\non august 28 , you sent a request to enter a spot ticket for september\r\nproduction on engage energy , meter # 5848 , 240 mmbtu / d . the ticket was\r\nentered as a purchase from coastal merchant energy , l . p . a volume of 304\r\nmmbtu flowed on meter # 5848 on 10 / 1 / 00 . should there be a spot purchase at\r\nmeter # 5848 in october ? please advise . thanks .\r\nbob\r\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - forwarded by robert cotten / hou / ect on 10 / 11 / 2000 10 : 45\r\nam - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\r\naimee lannou 10 / 11 / 2000 10 : 02 am\r\nto : robert cotten / hou / ect @ ect\r\ncc : daren j farmer / hou / ect @ ect , pat clynes / corp / enron @ enron\r\nsubject : meter 5848\r\nbob - there is flow at meter 5848 for 10 / 1 . in sept . it was on a gathering\r\ncontract on deal # 382621 for coastal merchant energy . could you please\r\ncheck to see if there should be a deal for october ?\r\nthanks .\r\naimee',ham
'Subject: re : rate for tenaska deal\r\ndaren ,\r\nthanks - - while i \' m certain i should know , i must confess that i do not know\r\nwhat cpi stands for ? ? ?\r\nsandi\r\ndaren j farmer\r\n10 / 16 / 2000 11 : 39 am\r\nto : sandi m braband / hou / ect @ ect , bob m hall / na / enron @ enron\r\ncc :\r\nsubject : re : rate for tenaska deal\r\nsandi ,\r\nsorry for just now getting back with you . i was out last week .\r\nthe rate ( $ . 04 / mmbtu ) will be charged on the greater of the volumes nominated\r\non the supply contracts or the actual deliveries to the plant . the fee will\r\nbe adjusted yearly based on cpi .\r\nbob - i could not remember if we stated the type of settlement on the\r\ndelivered volumes ( actuals or nominations ) . i think we should use actuals\r\ndue to possibility that the plant could over pull with out our knowledge on a\r\ndaily basis . we would receive the estimates / actuals on a lag and may have to\r\npurchase gas to offset the imbalance , even though the plant kept the noms at\r\nthe 45 , 000 base . i also think that if the plant does increase the nom , they\r\nare more likely to pull the additional volume rather than pulling less . do\r\nyou agree with this ?\r\nd\r\nfrom : sandi m braband on 10 / 10 / 2000 03 : 41 pm\r\nto : daren j farmer / hou / ect @ ect\r\ncc :\r\nsubject : rate for tenaska deal\r\ndaren ,\r\nwhen we met regarding the rate for the tenaska gas management agreement , you\r\nguys mentioned that it would be tied to an index - - could you restate for me\r\nhow that is to work - - it will start out 4 cents per mmbtu based on the greater\r\nof the volumes nominated through the supply contracts or the actual\r\ndeliveries to the plant . then the fee will vary month to month ? year to year ?\r\nbased on what index ?\r\nthanks ,\r\nsandi',ham
